# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# syniq-opr-app — .gitignore
#
# Android-only by design (plan §4.2), so this file carries no Xcode, CocoaPods or Ruby sections.
# If an iOS target is ever added, add them then — an ignore rule for a platform that does not
# exist only teaches the next reader that one does.
#
# ⚠ TWO RULES FROM loadindo-vendor ARE DELIBERATELY NOT COPIED. See "Not ignored, on purpose".
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnp/
.pnp.js

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.jsbundle

# ── Metro ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.metro-health-check*
metro-cache/

# ── Android ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
android/.gradle/
android/.idea/
android/.kotlin/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/captures/
android/local.properties
android/*.iml
.cxx/
*.hprof
*.apk
*.aab

# Signing material. `debug.keystore` is the shared, publicly-known debug key that ships with the
# Android SDK and MUST stay tracked — without it every developer signs debug builds with a
# different key and cannot upgrade over each other's installs.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
!android/app/debug.keystore

# ── Secrets & environment ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env

# ── Testing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# ── Editors & tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.orig
*.orig.*
*.bak

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*

# ── Temp ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.tmp
*.temp
tmp/
temp/

# ── OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NOT IGNORED, ON PURPOSE
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# 1. `**/env.ts` — loadindo-vendor ignores this, and copying that here would be a real bug.
#    It ignores it because ITS env.ts holds a live Google Maps API key. Ours holds a public base
#    URL and a timeout, nothing secret, and it is an ordinary source file that the app will not
#    compile without. An ignore rule that silently drops a tracked source file is exactly the
#    class of mistake that cost this programme ~50 ghost migrations when `*.sql` was ignored in
#    syniq-server. Secrets belong in `.env` (ignored above), never in a source file.
#
# 2. `package-lock.json` — committed. A handheld fleet must be reproducible build to build, and
#    an RN dependency graph is not stable without the lock.
#
# 3. The GENERATED files are committed and must stay so:
#      src/theme/tokens/colors.light.ts
#      src/theme/tokens/colors.dark.ts
#      src/theme/tokens/radius.ts
#      src/authz/permissions.generated.ts
#    Their generators (`npm run tokens:sync`, `npm run perms:sync`) read the SIBLING checkouts
#    ../syniq-web and ../syniq-server, which a CI runner or a fresh clone will not have. Ignoring
#    them would make this repo un-buildable anywhere those siblings are absent. The `:check`
#    halves of the same scripts are what keep them honest.



#